From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: Revert "Only preload SwiftShader in GPU sandbox init when allowed"

This reverts the gpu_init.cc change from
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7636200.

The GPU process enables MITIGATION_FORCE_MS_SIGNED_BINS once its sandbox
is initialized, so vk_swiftshader.dll has to be loaded before that if it
is going to be used at all. That CL made the preload conditional on
SwiftShader being requested explicitly, but WebGPU's fallback adapter on
Windows is SwiftShader over Vulkan (Dawn's D3D backends return no
adapters for forceFallbackAdapter), and WebGPUDecoderImpl still asks for
it when no D3D12 adapter is usable or the page passes
forceFallbackAdapter. The late load is rejected by Code Integrity; for
AppX/MSIX packaged apps the loader treats that as package tampering,
terminates the GPU process and marks the package as needing repair.

A narrower condition is proposed upstream at
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8286976; this
patch can be dropped once that or an equivalent lands.

diff --git a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_init.cc b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_init.cc
index 09780f226ffe3794550e40cc6c692167b5c0ca00..b353b108392657249f789b65de4f726458fc0cab 100644
--- a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_init.cc
+++ b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_init.cc
@@ -672,17 +672,7 @@ bool GpuInit::InitializeAndStartSandbox(base::CommandLine* command_line,
 
     base::FilePath module_path;
     if (base::PathService::Get(base::DIR_MODULE, &module_path)) {
-      // Preload vk_swiftshader.dll when SwiftShader may be needed:
-      // - IsSwiftShaderAllowed() covers ANGLE/GL flags like
-      //   --enable-unsafe-swiftshader and --use-angle=swiftshader.
-      // - use_webgpu_adapter covers --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader for
-      //   WebGPU fallback adapter selection.
-      // - DefaultForceFallbackAdapter() covers Graphite/Dawn using
-      //   SwiftShader via --skia-graphite-dawn-backend=swiftshader.
-      if (features::IsSwiftShaderAllowed(command_line) ||
-          gpu_preferences_.use_webgpu_adapter ==
-              WebGPUAdapterName::kSwiftShader ||
-          DawnContextProvider::DefaultForceFallbackAdapter()) {
+      {
         TRACE_EVENT("gpu,startup", "Load vk_swiftshader.dll");
         base::LoadNativeLibrary(module_path.Append(L"vk_swiftshader.dll"),
                                 nullptr);
